                <pb facs="1048" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2804a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Warren</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-07T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>134. Department’s No. 129, October 30, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>If Japanese Government does not object to delay Department would prefer awaiting
                    Stevens’ arrival in Washington before giving final consideration to point 4 of
                    Japanese instructions stated in your No. 172, October 17, 2 p.m. If Stevens
                    passes through Tokyo please consult with him on subject acquainting yourself
                    fully with the facts.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
